Topic 1: Single Inheritance
1. What is Single Inheritance?
Definition
Single inheritance means:
A child class inherits properties and methods from one parent class.


Key Points
One parent class → one child class


Child class can access:


Parent class variables


Parent class methods


Helps in code reusability


Reduces repeated code


Syntax
class parent_class:
    def __init__(self,p1,p2):
        self.p1=p1
        self.p2=p2
    def method_name(self):
        #implementation


class child_class(parent_class):
    def __init__(self,p3,p4):
        self.p3=p3
        self.p4=p4
    def method_name(self):
        #implementation
       


child_object=child_class(p1,p2)
child_object.method_name()



Topic 2: super() Method
What is super()?
Definition
super() is used inside a child class to call:
Parent class constructor (__init__)


Parent class methods


Why super() is Used?
To reuse parent class initialization


To avoid rewriting parent attributes in child class


To ensure parent class variables are properly created


Important Note
If we do not call super().__init__(), parent class variables will not be initialized automatically.

Example 1: Father and Son (Single Inheritance + super())
Code
class father:
    def __init__(self,surname,name):
        self.surname=surname
        self.father_name=name

    def display_surname(self):
        print("surname is ", self.surname)

    def display_father_name(self):
        print("The fathername is ", self.father_name)


class son(father):
    def __init__(self,name,surname,father_name):
        self.name=name
        super().__init__(surname,father_name)

    def display_name(self):
        print("name is ", self.name)


child_obj=son("john", "K","Rajesh")
child_obj.display_father_name()
child_obj.display_surname()
child_obj.display_name()


Explanation
Parent Class (father)
Stores:
surname


father_name


Provides methods:
display_surname()


display_father_name()


Child Class (son)
Stores:
name (child specific)


Uses:
super().__init__(surname,father_name) to initialize parent class variables


So the child object can access:
display_father_name()


display_surname()


display_name()



Topic 3: Library Example (Single Inheritance)
Example 2: Books and IssuedBooks
Code
class Books:
    def __init__(self,title,author):
        self.title=title
        self.author=author

    def display_books_details(self):
        print("The title of the book is ",self.title)
        print("The author of the book is ",self.author)


class IssuedBooks(Books):
    def __init__(self,title,author,issued_to,issued_date):
        self.issued_to=issued_to
        self.issued_date=issued_date
        super().__init__(title, author)

    def display_issued_books_details(self):
        print("The title of the book is ",self.title)
        print("The author of the book is ",self.author)
        print("The name of the person issued to is", self.issued_to)
        print("The date of issued is",self.issued_date)


IB=IssuedBooks("Python","John","Students","04-02-26")
IB.display_books_details()


Explanation
Parent Class: Books
Contains:
title


author


Method:
display_books_details()


Child Class: IssuedBooks
Adds:
issued_to


issued_date


Uses:
super().__init__(title, author) to initialize parent attributes



Topic 4: GitHub Branching (Team Workflow)
What is a Branch?
Definition
A branch is a separate copy of the project code where we can work independently without disturbing the main project.

Why Branching is Needed?
Real Scenario: Two Developers Working
If 2 developers work directly on main branch:
Both will modify the same files


When pushing code, conflicts may happen


Example:
Developer A updates login.py


Developer B updates the same login.py


When both push → Git gets confused which code is correct
 This creates a merge conflict.



How Branching Solves This Problem
Developer A creates branch: feature-login


Developer B creates branch: feature-ui


Both work independently


Later code is merged safely into main



Topic 5: Git Branch Commands
Branch Creation
git branch branch_name

Check Available Branches
git branch

Switch to Branch
git checkout branch_name

Create and Switch in One Command
git checkout -b branch_name

Push Branch to GitHub
git push origin branch_name


